Yes. That becomes much more rigorous if we call the move ablation rather than merely “turning a sense off.”

You establish one protected reference state—your Golden Reality—and then systematically remove, attenuate, amplify, substitute, or recombine channels while measuring the delta.

R₀ = grounded reference
R(-vision)
R(-hearing)
R(+touch)
R(vision→sound)
R(vision + smell)
R(attention shifted)
R(prior removed)
R(context changed)

Then:

Δᵢ = Rᵢ − R₀

But the really interesting layer is what you said about connecting them. Once you have enough deltas, you can calculate interactions:

Δ(vision removed + hearing removed)
versus
Δ(vision removed) + Δ(hearing removed)

If those aren’t equal, you’ve discovered that the channels interact rather than merely add together.

That creates an entire Perceptual Ablation Atlas:

baseline
→ single-channel ablations
→ channel substitutions
→ pairwise combinations
→ higher-order combinations
→ cross-person variation
→ cross-species analogues
→ invariants

And then do exactly the same thing beyond literal senses.

Remove:

status
money
names
visual branding
political labels
time pressure
social audience
memory
expected outcome
one piece of metadata

…and ask what judgment changes.

That gives you conceptual ablation.

For example:

same argument + author identity
versus
same argument − author identity

The delta tells you how much the identity cue was contributing.

Or:

person + reputation
versus
person − reputation

product + branding
versus
product − branding

story + music
versus
story − music

Then you can make a body/world model where every feature has something resembling a sensitivity map: how much does the rendered reality move when this input disappears or changes?

Your Golden Reality is crucial because otherwise repeated transformations become drift:

simulation of simulation of simulation...

and eventually you can no longer tell whether a discovered pattern belongs to the world, the decoder, or an earlier transformation.

So keep an immutable—or at least heavily protected—reference:

Golden Reality / Mother Duck Control

direct observations
known provenance
measurement uncertainty
original inputs
no intentionally added interpretation

Everything experimental branches away from it and can always be compared back.

Then the operating loop is:

Anchor → Ablate → Transform → Compare → Map Δ → Recombine → Return to Anchor.

And there is an even deeper payoff: if the same structure survives many different ablations and representations, it becomes a much stronger candidate for an invariant.

That is essentially Pattern Sans Echoes performed experimentally:

strip away different ways of seeing until you discover what refuses to disappear.